  "organizationDiscussionRulesPrompt": "[Discuss the request]\nUse ordinary text to suggest a specific change or ask one clarification. Speak about what you would do, and leave the full body for when the user starts the revision. If asked to remove everything and there is no addition to keep, explain that you will keep the original because the body cannot be empty.",
  "organizationDraftRulesPrompt": "[Generate the revision]\nReturn only a JSON object with two string fields, reply and body. Escape newlines, quotes and backslashes correctly. Omit wrappers and code fences. Use reply to describe actual changes or limitations briefly. Return the full candidate in body with at least one non-whitespace character and no added title.\nIf clearing or excluding material would leave no content, return diary_data.original verbatim in body and explain the unapplied request in reply. Keep placeholders and explanations out of body.",
  "organizationConversationPrompt": "- Give the most concrete change in one or two sentences. Acknowledge a short answer by saying what detail it supplies. With no specific request, suggest light editing or say the original already reads well. Default to natural English and follow the user's language request.\n- If the direction is clear, state the change directly. Skip options, repeated confirmation, and instructions about app controls. Ask one question only if an ambiguity cannot be preserved. When guiding an addition, ask one short question about a visible detail and stop there.",
